description: Keep title, brand, and Chinese fonts on separate tokens
alwaysApply: true
---

# Title vs brand fonts

Titles and the shop name use different CSS tokens. Changing one must never change the other.

- `--font-display` / `font-display`: display family for titles
- `.display-title` / `.section-title`: short page and section titles (uppercase + tracking). Use these for labels like Shop, FAQ, Cart, Themes
- Product names, cart line titles, and nav links stay in normal case with `font-display` only when needed
- `--font-logo` / `font-logo`: English brand name only (header logo and entrance brand)
- `--font-about-mark` / `font-about-mark`: Chinese marks for brand subtitle 小忆 (header logo) and about-page Chinese spans in non-zh locales (小忆, 孙义栋, and related characters; currently Ma Shan Zheng)
- `--font-mark` / `font-mark`: alias stack for Chinese marks (keep in sync with `--font-about-mark`)
- `--font-sans`: body copy and UI chrome

When the user asks to change the title font:
1. Update the display family in `nuxt.config.ts` `fonts.families` and `--font-display` in `app/assets/css/main.css`.
2. Do not edit `--font-logo`, `font-logo`, or brand markup in `AppLogo.vue` / `HeroBanner.vue`.
3. Do not edit `--font-mark`, `--font-about-mark`, or Ma Shan Zheng.

When the user asks to change the brand name font:
1. Update the logo family in `nuxt.config.ts` and `--font-logo` only (English "Little Memo").
2. Do not edit `--font-display`, title components, `--font-mark`, or `--font-about-mark`.

# Locale UI fonts

Chinese (`html[data-locale="zh"]` and related):
- Titles: **Ma Shan Zheng** via `--font-display`
- Body / UI chrome: **ZCOOL KuaiLe** via `--font-sans`

Korean (`html[data-locale="ko"]` and related):
- Titles: **Single Day** via `--font-display`
- Body / UI chrome: **Nunito Sans** for Latin, **Nanum Brush Script** for Korean glyphs via `--font-sans`
- Body size is slightly larger than the default locale (`1.2rem`)

Japanese (`html[data-locale="ja"]` and related):
- Titles: **Shippori Antique B1** via `--font-display`
- Body / UI chrome: **Nunito Sans** for Latin, **Kosugi Maru** for Japanese glyphs via `--font-sans`

For all CJK locales:
- English brand name stays `--font-logo` (Gaegu). Do not point logo at locale title fonts.
- Brand subtitle 小忆 in the header/logo uses `--font-about-mark`. Locale title/body overrides must never change `--font-mark` or `--font-about-mark`.

# Inline brand names in body copy

In running body copy (for example the about page), do not switch fonts for brand references:

- English **Little Memo**: keep `--font-sans`. Emphasize with `font-bold` and ink only. Never use `font-logo` inline in paragraphs.
- Chinese characters in zh locale (小忆, 忆, 义, 孙义栋, memory-word list items, and similar): keep the Chinese body font (`--font-sans` / ZCOOL KuaiLe). Emphasize with `font-bold` and ink only. Do not use `font-about-mark` / Ma Shan Zheng for those spans.
- Other locales still use `font-about-mark` for about-page Chinese spans so non-Chinese readers see the mark style.

Header/logo treatment stays separate: `AppLogo.vue` English name uses `font-logo`, and the brand subtitle 小忆 stays on `font-about-mark` in every locale, including zh.

These locale overrides live in `app/assets/css/main.css`. Changing the default (non-CJK) title or body font must not remove locale overrides unless the user asks.

# Chinese mark fonts stay locked

`--font-mark` (brand Chinese subtitle) and `--font-about-mark` (about-page Chinese) are independent of title and English brand font changes.

- Never change Ma Shan Zheng for marks, `--font-mark`, `--font-about-mark`, `font-mark`, `font-about-mark`, or the Chinese spans in `AppLogo.vue` / `about.vue` unless the user explicitly asks to change that specific Chinese font.
- Changing "the font", "titles", "brand", or "display" does not authorize touching either Chinese mark font.
- Only change brand Chinese when the user clearly asks for the header/logo Chinese subtitle font.
- Only change about Chinese when the user clearly asks for the about-page Chinese font.
- Only change Chinese locale title/body fonts when the user clearly asks about Chinese translations / zh locale fonts.
- Only change Korean locale title/body fonts when the user clearly asks about Korean translations / ko locale fonts.
- Only change Japanese locale title/body fonts when the user clearly asks about Japanese translations / ja locale fonts.

Never point `--font-display` and `--font-logo` at the same family unless the user explicitly asks for both.

# Panel roundness

Cards, panels, mats, FAQ boxes, newsletter, and gallery frames use `--radius-panel` (`0.375rem`, same as Tailwind `rounded-md`). Keep those surfaces on that token or `rounded-md`. Buttons, chips that are pills, badges, and tab pills stay `rounded-full` / `999px`.
